# Documentation

Document:

- purpose
- architecture
- decisions (ADRs)
- usage
- limitations
- examples

Avoid documenting obvious implementation details.

## Structure

```
docs/
  architecture/  agents/  skills/  conventions/  decisions/  templates/  plans/
```

## Requirements

- Every runtime agent and skill has a README.
- Important architecture choices use ADRs (`docs/decisions/`).
- Prefer linking to contracts/templates over duplicating prose.
- Update docs when behavior or contracts change.

Templates: `docs/templates/`
ADR template: `docs/templates/adr.md`
